{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793397047,"nonce":"UxZeGwWi7PuYHLoVnmy/YNLxtZw=","message":"Chosen fix: keep a session's typed imports across edits and retype only the edited module (the Haxe compiler server model).\n\nToday every edit of the open document makes new session inputs, so compile_file builds a fresh CompilationUnit and retypes the whole import graph (291 files, 216 s for Ashui's MarkupDisplay.hx on the NUC; BLADE is off for haxelib projects). A display compile repeats the same work.\n\nWith a persistent graph:\n- an edit removes the module's declarations, typed file and references from the live unit and re-lowers it; when its public signatures change, its dependents are retyped too;\n- a display request re-lowers the module with the cursor set against the same graph, and its result never replaces the analysis.\n\nThe missing primitive is removing one module from a live CompilationUnit. Folding the cursor into the analysis was rejected: it saves the second compile but each completion still waits a full analysis.","files":null}]}